From fb3bb214491733bc2be7a6d3b3cd7337705168d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:42:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tlc): per-half edge-effect correction from picked
 same-compound spots

Edge effect makes lanes near the plate edges run faster or slower than the
middle, which shifts Rf. The relative migration speed g(x) is fitted
separately for each half of the plate (either sign, either edge more).

- Pick spots that must have the same Rf in the Full plate view (compound
  groups, click again to remove). The correction is calculated from them
  and applied in Auto mode only when the picks agree (scatter <= 6 %),
  cover at least half the plate width and the curve exceeds the scatter.
- Without picks, an automatic estimate from repeated compounds is shown as
  a suggestion only; Force on applies it.
- Per half: Auto / Force on / Off, strength 0-100 %, diagnostic plot.
- Rf CSV gains edge_gain and rf_raw_1..5; raw Rf is kept next to corrected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
